  "scope": "Initial source branching and semantic rank produce whole-query instruction credit. All node compiler and actual checked edge branches derive it without a future trace or instruction count. Every actual yielded physical prefix consumes credit, including cold publication, demanded bodies, warm returns, and both protected finishes. Closed original roots with initial headroom, semantic physical readiness, and idle warm tables construct their own complete physical receipt, exact execute, and payload/allocation bounds at the initial instruction budget. No future Trace, WordRanges, entry counter, or desired result law is supplied to the initial endpoint. The semantic budget is mathematical and noncomputable; an executable syntax-only bound, general result-fed query sequences, constrained execution, convergence, concrete capacity, current adapters, and complete public Haskell correspondence remain open."
